  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Linear Discriminant Analysis** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_lda_classify(X1: list, X2: list) -> list:\n    a1, a2 = np.array(X1, dtype=float), np.array(X2, dtype=float)\n    m1, m2 = np.mean(a1, axis=0), np.mean(a2, axis=0)\n    sw = (a1 - m1).T @ (a1 - m1) + (a2 - m2).T @ (a2 - m2) + 1e-6 * np.eye(len(m1))\n    w = np.linalg.solve(sw, m1 - m2)\n    return np.round(w / np.linalg.norm(w), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
